1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:02,692
{happy}Hello, and welcome to Shah Spectrum.

2
00:00:02,692 --> 00:00:04,753
If you're new here, welcome.

3
00:00:04,753 --> 00:00:07,908
If you're back again, it's good to have you with us.

4
00:00:07,908 --> 00:00:11,825
{happy}What can one announcement do to a stock market?

5
00:00:11,825 --> 00:00:18,652
On Monday, a single announcement helped lift the S&P 500, an index of big American

6
00:00:18,652 --> 00:00:22,198
companies, by about five per cent in a day.

7
00:00:22,198 --> 00:00:25,399
That was its best day since April of last year.

8
00:00:25,399 --> 00:00:26,854
So did it fix anything?

9
00:00:26,854 --> 00:00:28,064
{happy}I'm Mittal Shah.

10
00:00:28,064 --> 00:00:30,956
Stay with me, and we'll separate what changed from what didn't.

11
00:00:30,956 --> 00:00:33,550
{fluent}First, what happened.

12
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:38,415
On Monday the twenty-third of November, Nvidia, the AI chip maker, announced that

13
00:00:38,415 --> 00:00:40,964
Jensen Huang is chief executive again.

14
00:00:40,964 --> 00:00:48,293
He is also back as president and as a member of the board, effective immediately.

15
00:00:48,293 --> 00:00:53,895
He had resigned earlier this month, and the finance chief, Colette Kress, had been

16
00:00:53,895 --> 00:00:56,225
running the company as interim chief executive.

17
00:00:56,225 --> 00:00:58,928
Interim means temporary.

18
00:00:59,414 --> 00:01:02,127
The board says it voted unanimously.

19
00:01:02,127 --> 00:01:06,938
It says it was satisfied with Huang's candor, meaning his openness, and with his

20
00:01:06,938 --> 00:01:08,339
ability to lead.

21
00:01:08,339 --> 00:01:14,247
It also says it received input from senior levels of the United States government,

22
00:01:14,247 --> 00:01:19,653
and is confident his return poses no national security risk.

23
00:01:20,090 --> 00:01:21,538
The board added two things.

24
00:01:21,538 --> 00:01:27,403
First, a new committee of independent directors to oversee trade compliance and

25
00:01:27,403 --> 00:01:28,897
national security risks.

26
00:01:28,897 --> 00:01:31,380
Second, a search for a chief compliance officer.

27
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:37,030
And an earlier investigation by independent directors continues.

28
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:42,557
It was opened after reports that Huang was the target of a foreign intelligence

29
00:01:42,557 --> 00:01:43,157
effort.

30
00:01:43,017 --> 00:01:44,564
Those reports remain unproven.

31
00:01:44,879 --> 00:01:45,769
Now, the market.

32
00:01:45,769 --> 00:01:48,278
Start with the week before.

33
00:01:48,278 --> 00:01:53,162
On Friday the twentieth, the Nasdaq, the index heavy with technology companies, fell

34
00:01:53,162 --> 00:01:56,974
about five per cent in one day.

35
00:01:56,974 --> 00:02:01,953
The S&P 500, which tracks five hundred of America's biggest listed companies, was

36
00:02:01,953 --> 00:02:06,460
down more than eleven per cent from its record on the sixth of October.

37
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:10,704
Market people call a fall of ten per cent or more a correction.

38
00:02:11,096 --> 00:02:12,511
Then Monday flipped it.

39
00:02:12,511 --> 00:02:18,422
By the close, the S&P 500 was up about five per cent, the Nasdaq up more than six

40
00:02:18,422 --> 00:02:23,800
per cent, and the Dow, an index of thirty big companies, up about three per cent.

41
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:27,728
All three had their best day since April twenty twenty-five.

42
00:02:27,728 --> 00:02:30,233
Nvidia's shares rose by about a third.

43
00:02:30,616 --> 00:02:33,412
Why could one announcement move so much?

44
00:02:33,412 --> 00:02:39,380
The S&P 500 and the Nasdaq give bigger companies more weight, so the biggest names

45
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:40,404
pull them hardest.

46
00:02:40,404 --> 00:02:45,192
When the biggest names in AI move together, the whole index feels it.

47
00:02:45,584 --> 00:02:48,407
But the fall was not only about one man.

48
00:02:48,407 --> 00:02:52,007
Earlier this month, the worry was politics and power bills.

49
00:02:52,007 --> 00:02:54,173
Behind it sits a bigger question:

50
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:59,601
will all the money companies are spending on AI chips, buildings and power ever pay

51
00:02:59,601 --> 00:03:00,201
off?

52
00:02:59,834 --> 00:03:04,905
By one news outlet's count, the S&P 500 had lost about eight trillion dollars of

53
00:03:04,905 --> 00:03:05,771
value by Friday.

54
00:03:05,771 --> 00:03:07,329
Monday won back about three trillion.

55
00:03:07,329 --> 00:03:12,001
That leaves it about five trillion short of its October record.

56
00:03:12,432 --> 00:03:15,028
So did Huang's return answer the question?

57
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:18,272
One fund chief investment officer said no:

58
00:03:18,272 --> 00:03:22,877
it does not answer the big questions about whether AI spending will pay off.

59
00:03:22,877 --> 00:03:24,055
That is a view, not a fact.

60
00:03:24,377 --> 00:03:25,507
What do we not know?

61
00:03:25,507 --> 00:03:30,151
The company gave no reason for the resignation.

62
00:03:30,151 --> 00:03:33,088
The investigation has published no findings.

63
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:36,774
And one day's rally does not tell us what comes next.

64
00:03:36,774 --> 00:03:37,853
{happy}To sum up:

65
00:03:37,853 --> 00:03:43,440
a rally followed one announcement, and the announcement changed who leads Nvidia.

66
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:46,846
It did not settle whether AI spending will pay off.

67
00:03:46,846 --> 00:03:50,377
{happy}This is news and explanation, not investment advice.

68
00:03:50,377 --> 00:03:53,384
Before you go, we covered this story earlier:

69
00:03:53,384 --> 00:03:54,809
"AI shares sell-off:

70
00:03:54,809 --> 00:04:00,593
data centres and the election", on the sixth of November, and "Nvidia reports

71
00:04:00,593 --> 00:04:04,541
results days after its CEO resigned", on the sixteenth.

72
00:04:04,541 --> 00:04:06,609
Both links are in the description.

73
00:04:06,609 --> 00:04:09,718
Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode!

